## 4. Target Users

### 4.1 Primary Persona — "Priya"

- **Age:** 25–35
- **Role:** Product manager, freelancer, startup operator, consultant
- **Behavior:** Intelligent, self-aware, wants to be organized, has tried multiple productivity tools
- **Pain Point:** Her reality changes daily — some days she has deep focus blocks, others she's in back-to-back meetings. No current app accounts for this variance
- **Quote:** *"I know what I need to do. I just can't figure out what to do *right now*."*

### 4.2 Secondary Persona — "Team Lead Arjun"

- **Age:** 28–40
- **Role:** Engineering lead, startup founder, team manager
- **Behavior:** Manages both personal tasks and shared team obligations
- **Pain Point:** Can't see what his team is genuinely blocked on versus what's just being avoided
- **Quote:** *"I don't want to micromanage. I just want to know when something is actually stuck."*

### 4.3 Anti-Persona (Who We Are NOT Building For)

- Power users who want highly configurable systems (they have Notion and Obsidian)
- Enterprise IT buyers who want deep integrations (we'll get there, not in Phase 1–2)
- Users who want a social/gamified productivity experience

