## 5. Product Overview and Feature Set

### 5.1 Feature Hierarchy

**Must Have (Phase 1 — MVP)**
- Mood-state based task surfacing
- Task input with context tagging
- Active task cap (15 tasks)
- Basic task CRUD (Create, Read, Update, Delete)
- Backlog / Someday list

**Should Have (Phase 2)**
- Friction mapping and behavioral nudges
- Sunday Reckoning conversation flow
- Sub-task generation from friction triggers
- Person-linked follow-up tasks

**Could Have (Phase 3)**
- True Context Moment (location + calendar + time)
- Calendar integration (Google, Outlook)
- Android and iOS native apps
- Team workspace and shared task visibility

**Won't Have (V1)**
- Recurring task templates
- Integrations with Slack, Jira, Notion (post-MVP)
- Analytics dashboards
- Custom themes and views

