## 6. Detailed Feature Specifications

### 6.1 Mood-State Entry Screen

**Description:** The first screen a user sees upon opening the app each session. A single contextual question that calibrates which tasks are surfaced.

**User Flow:**
1. User opens app
2. Presented with: *"How are you walking in today?"*
3. Selects one of five states:
   - 🔥 Focused and sharp — deep work available
   - 🪫 Running on low — need easy wins
   - ⚡ In between things — have 20–30 minutes
   - 🎨 Creative headspace — good for brainstorming/writing
   - ✅ Just want to clear small things — errands and quick tasks
4. App transitions to Focused Task View showing 4–6 matched tasks
5. Mood state persists for the session unless manually changed

**Task-to-Mood Mapping:**
- Each task carries a hidden "required state" tag — set by the user at input, adjusted by ML over time
- Mapping is fuzzy: "Focused and sharp" also shows "In between things" tasks if the focused list has fewer than 4 items
- User can override and see full list via "Show everything" toggle (available but not prominent)

**Design Requirements:**
- Mood selection UI must take under 3 seconds to complete
- No more than 5 options — ever
- Friendly, non-corporate language — no "Priority Matrix" type framing
- Accessible: full screen tap targets, not small buttons

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- [ ] Mood-state screen appears on every cold open and after 4+ hours of inactivity
- [ ] Task list updates immediately upon mood selection with no perceptible lag
- [ ] "Show everything" is available but requires deliberate action
- [ ] Selected mood is stored locally and used for pattern analysis (on-device only)

