### 6.3 Focused Task View

**Description:** The primary home screen of the app. Not a full list — a curated, mood-matched surface of 4–6 tasks.

**Layout:**
- Task cards, not list rows — each card has task name, estimated duration, and a subtle context tag
- Top of screen shows current mood state with easy one-tap change option
- Cards are dismissible left (snooze to later today) and right (mark complete)
- Below the focused cards: a subtle "X more tasks in your list" link — visible but not prominent

**Task Card Content:**
- Task name (primary, large)
- Duration estimate (secondary, small)
- Friction indicator (Phase 2): a subtle visual cue — not an alarm, just a quiet dot — if this task has been skipped before
- Person tag if applicable

**Interaction Design:**
- Completing a task: right swipe → satisfying animation → new task from matched mood slides in
- Snoozing a task: left swipe → "When should I resurface this?" → Later today / Tomorrow morning / This weekend
- Tapping a task: opens detail view with sub-tasks, notes, and history

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- [ ] Focused view never shows more than 6 tasks
- [ ] Completing a task triggers a micro-animation that feels rewarding (not just a checkmark disappearing)
- [ ] Snooze options are time-contextual — "this weekend" doesn't appear on a Monday at 9 AM if you have a busy schedule
- [ ] View reloads without full screen refresh when a task is completed

