### 6.5 Sunday Reckoning

**Description:** A weekly conversational review that helps users clear zombie tasks, re-commit to what matters, and start Monday with an honest, clean list.

**Trigger:**
- Notification at 7:00 PM local time every Sunday
- Optional: user can reschedule trigger to Saturday evening or Sunday morning in settings
- If user doesn't open it Sunday, surfaces as a gentle banner on Monday morning

**Conversation Flow:**
The Reckoning is a scripted conversational UI — warm, friendly tone. It is NOT a generative AI chat.

**Opening message:**
*"Hey, let's spend 3 minutes getting ready for the week ahead. No judgment — just honesty."*

**Flow for each flagged task (tasks that were moved, skipped 2+ times, or not touched in 7 days):**

> *"You moved '[task name]' [X] times this week."*
> *"What's the real story here?"*

Options:
- **I'll do it this week** — task stays active, friction score resets
- **Schedule a specific time** — opens a time-picker, blocks 30 minutes in calendar (Phase 3+)
- **I'm waiting on someone** — converts to follow-up task
- **Honestly, it's not important anymore** — moves to someday or deletes
- **It's done, just forgot to check it** — marks complete

**Closing:**
After all flagged tasks are processed:
*"Nice. You've got [X] things on your active list. You're ready for the week."*
If X > 12: gentle nudge — *"That's a full plate. Want to pick your top 3 priorities so you know where to start Monday morning?"*

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- [ ] Reckoning only surfaces tasks that meet the flagging criteria (moved 2+ times, or untouched for 7 days)
- [ ] Conversation completes in under 4 minutes for a typical user (tested with 5–8 flagged tasks)
- [ ] All decisions made in the Reckoning take immediate effect — no "save changes" step
- [ ] Skipping the Reckoning entirely is allowed — no guilt-tripping language if user dismisses
- [ ] Reckoning state is saved if interrupted — user can resume where they left off

