### 6.6 True Context Moment — Location + Calendar Intelligence (Phase 3)

**Description:** Smart, multi-signal notifications that only fire when a task is *genuinely actionable right now*.

**Signal Inputs:**
- GPS location (with permission)
- Calendar free/busy status (with integration)
- Time of day
- Task duration estimate
- Device usage pattern (laptop open = active work mode, phone only = mobile mode)

**True Context Moment Logic:**
A location-linked task notification fires only when ALL of the following are true:
1. User is within defined radius of relevant location (e.g., pharmacy, bank, specific office)
2. Calendar shows a free block of at least [task duration estimate] + 10 minutes
3. Current time is between 8 AM and 8 PM
4. Task has not been snoozed in the last 4 hours

**Device Behavior Rules (no location required):**
- Laptop opened after 9 PM → hide tasks requiring 60+ minutes, surface only ≤30-minute tasks
- App opened between 9–11 AM on a calendar-free morning → surface top deep work task with: *"You have a clear morning. Want to lock in on [task]?"*
- First app open on a Monday → show Sunday Reckoning if not completed, otherwise show weekly intent summary

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- [ ] Location data is processed on-device, never stored on servers
- [ ] Calendar integration is OAuth-based (Google Calendar v1, Outlook Phase 3b)
- [ ] All three conditions must be simultaneously true for a location notification to fire
- [ ] User can set "quiet hours" that override all context notifications
- [ ] Notification includes task name, estimated time needed, and a one-tap "Not now — remind me next time I'm nearby"

