## 8. Privacy and Data Architecture

This is a core product principle, not just a legal requirement.

### 8.1 On-Device Data (Never Transmitted)
- Task content and names
- Mood state selections
- Behavioral friction scores
- Location data
- Calendar event content

### 8.2 Server-Side Data (Anonymized, Aggregated)
- App session count (no content)
- Feature usage frequency
- Completion rate metrics (task marked complete = 1, no task content)
- Crash reports

### 8.3 Team Data (Encrypted, User-Controlled)
- Shared task names and status — stored encrypted, users can export and delete at any time
- No team data is used for product analytics or ML training without explicit opt-in

### 8.4 Privacy Principles
- No task content ever leaves the device for individual users
- On-device ML model runs locally using TensorFlow Lite
- Users can export all their data as JSON at any time
- Account deletion removes all server-side data within 24 hours, with confirmation

