## 9. Launch and Go-to-Market Strategy

### 9.1 Phase 1 Launch — Closed Beta (Month 1–3)
- 200 users, manually recruited from Hyderabad startup community, ProductHunt, and indie hacker communities
- Web app only — no App Store/Play Store listing
- Direct Slack/WhatsApp group with beta users for daily feedback
- Weekly founder office hours — 30-minute video calls with 5 users per week

### 9.2 Phase 2 Launch — Public Web Beta (Month 4–6)
- ProductHunt launch targeting Top 5 Product of the Day
- Written launch story on Substack and shared on LinkedIn — framing: *"We built a todo app that takes responsibility for your completion rate. Here's what we learned from 200 users."*
- Target communities: r/productivity, r/startups, Indie Hackers, Twitter/X productivity creators
- Referral program: invite 3 friends → unlock Team features free for 30 days

### 9.3 Phase 3 Launch — Mobile App (Month 7–9)
- Android first (Google Play Store)
- iOS 6 weeks later (App Store)
- ASO (App Store Optimization) focused on: "task completion app," "todo app that works," "productivity for busy professionals"
- PR angle: completion rate data from beta — *"Our users complete 72% of their tasks. The average app user completes 41%."*

