## 11. Success Metrics

### 11.1 North Star Metric
**7-day task completion rate** — percentage of active tasks marked complete within 7 days of creation

- Phase 1 target: ≥ 60% (vs. industry ~41%)
- Phase 2 target: ≥ 68%
- Phase 3 target: ≥ 75%

### 11.2 Supporting Metrics

**Engagement:**
- D7 retention: ≥ 55% (industry average for productivity apps: ~30%)
- D30 retention: ≥ 35%
- Daily active users / Monthly active users ratio: ≥ 0.45

**Product Health:**
- Average tasks completed per user per week
- Friction intervention acceptance rate (did the user take action on the suggestion?)
- Sunday Reckoning completion rate (% of users who complete the full flow)
- Task cap enforcement events per user per week (indicates active prioritization)

**Business:**
- Free to paid conversion rate: target 8% in month 6
- Monthly recurring revenue (MRR) growth: 20% month-over-month through end of Year 1
- Net Promoter Score: target ≥ 50 by end of Phase 2

### 11.3 Anti-Metrics (Things We Explicitly Do NOT Optimize For)
- Total tasks added (we don't want more tasks, we want more completed tasks)
- Time spent in app (we want efficient sessions, not addictive engagement)
- Notification volume (fewer, higher-quality notifications is the goal)

